    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0245" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/4782: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-03T20:00:00+01:00">July 3, 1936—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 3—5:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. The Mexican delegation withdrew from the Bureau of the Assembly<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d179-f1"/> this afternoon and presented a formal communication to
                    the President<anchor n="3" xml:id="d179-f2"/> to the effect that it could not
                    countenance the course of events being followed in the League and therefore
                    ceased to participate in the consideration of the Italo-Ethiopian dispute.</p>
                <p>The Bureau faced by widely divergent views is still desperately engaged <pb
                        facs="0246" n="181" xml:id="pg181"/> in an endeavor to draft a three point
                    resolution to be placed before the Assembly on sanctions, the Argentine
                    declaration, and League reforms.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d179-f1" n="2" xml:id="d179-f1-content">
                <p>The Bureau of the Assembly, also known as the General Committee of the Assembly,
                    was responsible for the coordination and direction of the Assembly’s work with
                    functions corresponding to those of a steering committee.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d179-f2" n="3" xml:id="d179-f2-content">
                <p>League of Nations, <hi rendition="#italic">Official Journal</hi>, Special
                    Supplement No. 151, p. 104.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
